{"id":"0b618255959ff4bc","group":"27","path":"27/27-df-dnf.md","title":"Disjunctive normal form","display":"df-dnf — Disjunctive normal form","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-df-dnf","aliases":["27-df-dnf"],"display":"df-dnf — Disjunctive normal form","depends_on":["[[27-df-term]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_section":"§1.4 Definition 1.10 and empty-family convention","source_printed_pages":"15","source_pdf_pages":"39","verification_status":"source-statement-checked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-df-dnf"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-df-dnf</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-dnf — Disjunctive normal form"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e065076d6b51508e\" href=\"?note=e065076d6b51508e\" title=\"27-df-term\">27-df-term</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§1.4 Definition 1.10 and empty-family convention"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"15"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"39"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Term}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Term}_n\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"e065076d6b51508e\" href=\"?note=e065076d6b51508e\" title=\"27-df-term\">27-df-term</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D\\subseteq\\mathrm{Term}_n\">\\(D\\subseteq\\mathrm{Term}_n\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\\in\\mathbb B^n\">\\(a\\in\\mathbb B^n\\)</span>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\coloneqq\\mathcal P(\\mathrm{Term}_n),\\qquad\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n(D)\\coloneqq\\left\\{\\left(a,1-\\prod_{T\\in D}(1-T(a))\\right)\\mid a\\in\\mathbb B^n\\right\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\coloneqq\\mathcal P(\\mathrm{Term}_n),\\qquad\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n(D)\\coloneqq\\left\\{\\left(a,1-\\prod_{T\\in D}(1-T(a))\\right)\\mid a\\in\\mathbb B^n\\right\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"⟦ D⟧_{\\vee}\\coloneqq\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n(D),\\qquad\\prod_{T\\in\\emptyset}(1-T(a))\\coloneqq1.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[⟦ D⟧_{\\vee}\\coloneqq\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n(D),\\qquad\\prod_{T\\in\\emptyset}(1-T(a))\\coloneqq1.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Term_n 有 3^n 个元素，所以每个 DNF 项集自动有限。项、文字的次序及重复在本表示中被商去；原书也在规范表示中忽略次序。用 EvalDNF 与 EvalCNF 区分同为集合的表示，尤其避免空集求值歧义。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-term","status":"resolved","id":"e065076d6b51508e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-term]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-term","status":"resolved","id"